// RunCode Runs a cell of Python in a build as a notebook does, in a Jupyter kernel it keeps running for the cell's `context`: variables, imports and functions stay for the next cell. Returns what it printed, its values and displays (text, HTML, images such as charts), and its exception with its traceback. The context's kernel starts on its first cell. A cell past `timeoutSeconds` is interrupted and its context kept. Refused 409 `kernel_not_installed` when the image has no ipykernel. A paused build is resumed first.
